    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "When a major power plant in the Visayas region failed, it triggered a grid incident that left the island group on high alert. The power grid managers and government authorities had to order emergency load shedding as a grid stabilization measure, resulting in a major power shortfall of over 950 megawatts for everyone in the area. This sudden energy deficit, driven by high summer demand straining the system, shows how a single equipment failure can disrupt daily life for ordinary people who depend on reliable electricity.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The recent blackout in the Visayas region stems from a power unit failing, adding to ongoing shutdowns at other plants. High summer demand strained the system to its limit, leading authorities to mandate power cuts to prevent a bigger outage. This energy deficit left hundreds of thousands of homes without power, a huge loss for ordinary people just trying to keep cool during the seasonal heat.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "why-1",
          "why-2",
          "how-2",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.78
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "Critical equipment let us down when a machine broke down, and the system couldn't handle everyone needing power at once. The power managers issued a warning, but rolling blackouts hit our community in the Visayas anyway because the grid failed to stabilize. Enough electricity to power hundreds of thousands of homes was gone—a stark reminder of how vulnerable everyday infrastructure is when demand spikes.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
